+{"status": "in_progress", "id": "DOC-3", "title": "operator path: document daemon lifecycle, port, pid/log location, orphan + corrupt-db recovery", "detail": {"fingerprint": "462d6fea38be5b1a9d3713f02aec94305d4ddebc57e65db368cde1ecbaaf30c7"}, "priority": "P4", "source": null, "reasoning": "Operator path gap (3am reader). Command run: ./bin/speclang status -> prints \"Daemon: Not running\" when the daemon is down and nothing else; neither docs/troubleshooting.md nor README tells an operator how to reach that state on purpose or what the recovery ladder is. No operator runbook exists in the repo (ls docs/ -> API_REFERENCE, BOOTSTRAP_PLAN, CASCADE_DEMO, CHANGELOG, CONTEXT, COORDINATOR, DOGFOODING, MASTER_GUIDE, NORTH_STAR, PRD.html, PY_SPEC_CONCEPT, layers.md, prompts/, troubleshooting.md, user-flows.md + archive/ + dogfood/; no runbook/OPERATIONS file).\nLive evidence for what the runbook must cover:\n- port: `speclang start --help` -> \"-p, --port <port>  Dashboard port (default: \"3000\")\"; 3000 collides with other local services and the flag appears in no doc (grep -rn \"\\-\\-port\" README.md GETTING-STARTED.md PACKAGING.md -> only PACKAGING.md mentions a port in passing). Pending QA row DF-SPECLANG-5 already names port collision for the RUNTIME side; this row is the operator DOC (how to change it).\n- PID/lifecycle: `speclang daemon --help` -> start/stop/status; `speclang stop` docs absent; the daemon's pid/log location is documented nowhere (MCP_LOG_FILE exists but is undocumented - see the env-var row).\n- stale/leftover daemons: a leaked `speclangd start --config=.speclangrc` child was observed reparented to systemd --user running hours after its parent test suite exited (see the foreman's own incident notes) - an operator has no doc telling them to `ps -o pid,ppid,etime,cmd` and kill it.\n- corrupted state: `.speclang/speclang.db` corruption is silently tolerated (pending QA-SPECLANG-5: build/status exit 0 on a truncated db) - the runbook must state the current (missing) integrity check and the safe reset procedure (delete .speclang/speclang.db and let the daemon rebuild).\nARTIFACT: docs/OPERATIONS.md (new) OR a \"Running SpecLang\" section in docs/troubleshooting.md.\nREADER: operator.\nACCEPT: an operator with no chat history can, from the repo root, find: how to start/stop/status the daemon, how to change the dashboard port, where the daemon writes its pid + log, how to find and kill an orphaned speclangd, and what to do when .speclang/speclang.db is corrupt - each with the exact command and its expected output.", "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-09-27T01:15:30.546264+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-16T22:51:21.866767+00:00", "acceptance": "At least one non-archive doc under docs/ carries the full daemon operator path: python3 -c \"import glob;oks=[f for f in glob.glob('docs/*.md') if all(s in open(f).read() for s in ('daemon.pid','daemon.log','3000'))];print('OK' if oks else 'FAIL');print(oks)\" prints OK and lists a file, and the same lookup restricted to the three daemon subcommands also returns a file: python3 -c \"import glob;need=['speclang daemon start','speclang daemon stop','speclang daemon status'];good=[f for f in glob.glob('docs/*.md') if all(s in open(f).read() for s in ('daemon.pid','daemon.log','3000')) and all(n in open(f).read() for n in need)];print('OK' if good else 'FAIL');print(good)\" prints OK with a non-empty file list. Values are the verified source defaults: port 3000 (src/daemon/daemon-cli.ts:40), pid .speclang/daemon.pid (daemon-cli.ts:47), log .speclang/daemon.log (src/daemon/config.ts:35).", "foreman_note": "Doc-severity re-triage 2026-10-27 per Bane ruling 2026-09-30 (documentation findings are P4, P5 for polish — never P1-P3): priority P2 -> P4. This is a POLICY change, not a new assessment; the finding is unchanged and re-verified this tick.\n\nRe-verified live: `./bin/speclang start --help` prints \"-p, --port <port>  Dashboard port (default: \\\"3000\\\")\" and `./bin/speclang status` prints only \"Daemon: Not running\" when down; no non-archive doc under docs/ carries daemon.pid / daemon.log / port 3000 (grep of docs/*.md), so the operator path is still undocumented.\n\nLeft at P4 rather than lower because a reader who needs the runbook has no pointer at all; not raised above P4 because the daemon commands the README names DO run (this is missing documentation, not a documented path that is broken — the P1 exception does not apply).", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/speclang-DOC-3", "branch": "wt/DOC-3", "sessions": ["SpecLang-docs-2026-11-16-22-47-48"]}
+{"status": "in_progress", "id": "DOC-4", "title": "README Agent Roles table names a nonexistent agent and omits two shipped ones", "detail": {"fingerprint": "7ecd27e37cc8d6342f92388305566f36da891bc22720df0963b86584741e8143"}, "priority": "P4", "source": null, "reasoning": "Rot, high severity because README contradicts itself in the same file. Command run: ./bin/speclang --help -> 21 commands; README CLI table (README.md:49-71) -> also 21 rows, but the row sets differ.\nMISSING from README's table (present in `--help`): `compile` (README:60 merges it into \"`build` / `compile [files...]`\" so the literal token `compile` is documented as a bare command - it IS an alias, so this half is fine), and NOTHING else missing.\nINVENTED in README's table (not in `--help`): README.md:445 \"- **Agent definitions**: Complete for all 5 roles\" while the tree it sits in (README:389-392) lists a 5-row table whose ROWS do not match the shipped files. Live: `ls .opencode/agents/` -> README.md, speclang-code-gen.md, speclang-coordinator.md, speclang-simulator-verify.md, speclang-simulator.md, speclang-spec-writer.md, speclang-verifier.md = 6 agent definitions + README.\nREADME's Agent Roles table (README.md:383-389) documents `@speclang-test-writer` and `@speclang-verifier`, and does NOT mention `@speclang-simulator` or `@speclang-simulator-verify`, both of which ship. A reader is told there is a test-writer agent file (there is not) and is never told about the two simulator agents.\nARTIFACT: README.md \"Agent Roles\" section (README.md:381-392).\nREADER: developer.\nACCEPT: the Agent Roles table lists exactly the agent definition files present in .opencode/agents/ (6 agents; excluding the README), the \"5 roles\" count is corrected, and no row names an agent file that does not exist.", "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-09-27T01:15:30.562311+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-16T22:51:22.308114+00:00", "acceptance": "Every agent named in the README '### Agent Roles' table resolves to a real agent file, and both shipped simulator agents are documented: awk '/^### Agent Roles/{f=1} /^### File Structure/{f=0} f' README.md | grep -oE '@speclang-[a-z-]+' | tr -d '@' | sort -u | while read -r a; do test -f \".opencode/agents/$a.md\" || echo \"MISSING $a\"; done | tee /tmp/acc-doc4.txt | grep -c MISSING; prints 0 and exits 1 (grep -c prints 0), while grep -c '@speclang-simulator-verify' README.md prints at least 1 and the Agent Roles table contains a row whose name also matches grep -cE '^\\| `@speclang-simulator`' README.md printing 1.", "foreman_note": "Doc-severity re-triage 2026-10-27 per Bane ruling 2026-09-30 (documentation findings are P4, P5 for polish — never P1-P3): priority P2 -> P4. POLICY change, not a new assessment; the finding is unchanged and re-verified this tick.\n\nRe-verified live: `ls .opencode/agents/` -> README.md, speclang-code-gen.md, speclang-coordinator.md, speclang-simulator-verify.md, speclang-simulator.md, speclang-spec-writer.md, speclang-verifier.md = 6 agent definitions plus README (no speclang-test-writer.md). `grep -n 'speclang-test-writer' README.md` -> README.md:216 and README.md:388 (the Agent Roles table), and README.md:445 still reads \"Agent definitions: Complete for all 5 roles\". The row's acceptance test (every @speclang-* named in the Agent Roles table resolves to .opencode/agents/<name>.md) is still the right gate.\n\nHeld at P4 rather than P5 because the table names an agent file that does not exist, so a reader who follows it invokes something that resolves to nothing; NOT raised to P1 because this is a prose/table defect, not a documented install/start/login path that fails.", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/speclang-README-1", "branch": "wt/README-1", "sessions": ["SpecLang-docs-2026-11-16-22-47-48"]}
+{"status": "in_progress", "id": "DOC-5", "title": "README Quick Start: _index.json entry count wrong and the documented --generate step dirties a tracked file", "detail": {"fingerprint": "e2cdaf0baafb4f35fc1d5737de9bb6eecc4777d254e370e351db7e17276ef587"}, "priority": "P4", "source": null, "reasoning": "Rot + a downstream trap. README.md:285-294 (Quick Start, \"Verify Everything Works\") says: \"The spec index (_index.json) is regenerated by the test suite; it currently holds 466 entries (verified 2026-08-13). The generator is explicit-mode only: a bare `python3 scripts/generate_index.py` prints usage and exits without writing anything. Use `--generate` to (re)write the index\".\nLive reality (measured this tick):\n- `python3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('/home/kara/speclang/_index.json'));print(len(d['specs']))\"` -> 464 entries, and the file's own `generated` field says \"2026-07-29T01:49:45.520ZZ\" - the README's \"466 (verified 2026-08-13)\" matches neither, and the file has not been regenerated since 2026-07-29 (git log -1 -- _index.json -> d4dd1b2c \"style: prettier format\").\n- The 466 number only appears when the generator runs over the live tree: `python3 scripts/generate_index.py --generate` output was \"Found 475 spec files / Created _index.json / - Specs: 466 / - References: 1263\". So the README quotes the generator's number while the committed file holds 464 - the committed artifact (what a reader actually opens) disagrees with the doc.\n- TRAP: that same documented command is a WRITE, not a check, and the README presents it under \"Verify Everything Works\" next to read-only steps. Running it modified the TRACKED file: `git diff --stat _index.json` -> 1 file changed, 16346 insertions(+), 10904 deletions(-) (475 files found vs 447 tracked .spec.md / 449 incl .scl, i.e. it swept untracked scratch spec copies). The foreman had to `git checkout -- _index.json` to undo it. Any contributor following Quick Start verbatim lands a 27k-line diff they did not intend.\nARTIFACT: README.md Quick Start step 4 (README.md:284-295).\nACCEPT: README states the entry count that the COMMITTED _index.json holds (or the file is regenerated in the same commit so the two agree), and the step is labelled as a write that dirties a tracked file, with the read-only alternative (`--validate`/`--tree`/`--impact`/`--graph`) named as the actual verification path.", "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-09-27T01:15:30.578947+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-16T22:51:22.352817+00:00", "acceptance": "Two checks from repo root: (1) `python3 scripts/generate_index.py --generate --output /tmp/index-check.json` exits 0 and `python3 -c \"import json;a=json.load(open('/tmp/index-check.json'))['specs'];b=json.load(open('_index.json'))['specs'];print('OK' if a==b else 'FAIL')\"` prints OK, so regenerating leaves `git status --porcelain _index.json` empty (the documented step no longer dirties a tracked file); (2) `python3 -c \"import json,re;n=len(json.load(open('_index.json'))['specs']);m=[int(x) for x in re.findall(r'(\\d+) entries',open('README.md').read())];print('OK %d'%n if m and all(v==n for v in m) else 'FAIL %s'%m)\"` prints 'OK 464' — the Quick Start entry count matches the real index.", "foreman_note": "Doc-severity re-triage 2026-11-03 (readme audit lane, tick speclang-readme-2026-11-03-15-46-12) per Bane ruling 2026-09-30: documentation findings are P4 (P5 for polish), never P1-P3. POLICY change only, not a new assessment — the finding is unchanged and still reproduces on the published tip 4cb5bbfb (README.md:287 '466 entries' vs committed _index.json).", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/speclang-README-1", "branch": "wt/README-1", "sessions": ["SpecLang-docs-2026-11-16-22-47-48"]}
+{"status": "in_progress", "id": "README-1", "title": "README documents a dead run command: npx ts-node crashes (ts-node 10.9.2 incompatible with typescript 7)", "detail": {"fingerprint": "913cb8de79e66c0b1da1ede502819d17ad39a8ebc5b2b3e31875b89a510badb8"}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "README health sweep 2026-09-27 (readme audit lane). README.md:367-369 documents this exact command:\n  npx ts-node examples/hello-world/index.ts\n  # Output: Hello, World!\n\nCommand run: cd /home/kara/speclang && npx ts-node examples/hello-world/index.ts\nActual output: RC=1, crash before any code runs:\n  /home/kara/speclang/node_modules/ts-node/dist/configuration.js:91\n  TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'fileExists')\n      at readConfig (.../ts-node/dist/configuration.js:91:33)\n  Root cause: ts-node ^10.9.2 is incompatible with typescript ^7.0.2 (devDependencies, package.json:85-86). ts-node 10.9.x supports TS up to 5.x; it dereferences the new TS API shape and crashes at config load.\n  The documented promised output \"Hello, World!\" never appears.\n\nFix: replace the ts-node command with one that runs, verified alternatives this tick:\n  npx tsx examples/hello-world/index.ts   (tsx current major supports TS 7; verify before merging)\n  or compile-and-run: node --experimental-strip-types  (verify)\n  or: npx tsc && node dist/examples/hello-world/index.js (verify)\nPick whichever passes in CI, update README.md:367 and the twin command at README.md:374 (same ts-node invocation on the spec-tree path), and note the typescript 7 incompatibility.", "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-09-27T02:01:46.703403+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-16T22:51:22Z", "foreman_note": "Re-verified 2026-10-12: crash still reproduces exactly (ts-node 10.9.2 vs typescript ^7.0.2, TypeError at configuration.js:91). PRIORITY LEFT AT P1 per re-triage rule: a documented install/run command that does not work is a functional defect wearing docs clothing (and the crash is the README's own promised Hello World path). Additional evidence this tick: npx tsx works as replacement on BOTH README.md:367 and :374 ('Hello, World!' rc=0, tsx not yet in devDependencies).", "acceptance": "grep -c 'npx ts-node' README.md prints 0 and exits 1, and the example run command that replaces the two 'npx ts-node' lines (README lines ~367 and ~374) exits 0 when extracted from the README code block and run from repo root.", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/speclang-README-1", "branch": "wt/README-1", "sessions": ["SpecLang-docs-2026-11-16-22-47-48"]}
