installed checkout and FALSE in a fresh clone. FIX must pin the command AND the condition, e.g. \"npm test -> 1826 passed | 58 skipped as of 2026-10-27 (checkout with git hooks installed; a fresh clone skips 7 CI-005 tests - see README-16)\".\n\nEvidence artifacts: /home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/readme/speclang/fulltest.log, ci005-probe.log, evidence-2026-10-27.md. Related: QA-SPECLANG-3 (pending) owns the OTHER fresh-clone-red mechanism (tests spawning bin/speclang).\n\nRe-verified 2026-11-16 by the readme audit lane (the '4 failed | 1822 passed' state README-2 was filed against on 09-27 no longer reproduces): npm test in /home/kara/speclang -> 'Test Files 97 passed | 4 skipped (101)' / 'Tests 1826 passed | 58 skipped (1884)' rc=0, matching README:90 verbatim; npx tsc --noEmit -> rc=0 (README-9 already recorded this). The count is TRUE for a fully provisioned checkout and FALSE for a stranger: in a fresh  + npm install, npm test reports 'Test Files 5 failed | 92 passed | 4 skipped (101)' / 'Tests 38 failed | 1781 passed | 65 skipped (1884)' (causes tracked separately: DF-SPECLANG-7 better-sqlite3 native binding blocked by npm>=12 install-scripts, README-16 git-hook step missing). Remaining actionable ask is unchanged and is the fix README-9 already prescribed: replace the bare numbers at README.md:90, :451, :534 with the pinning form 'verified 2026-11-16 on <node/npm> — command: npm test -> Tests 1826 passed | 58 skipped (1884); a fresh clone reports 38 failures until native deps are built', so the sentence cannot silently rot. This is a doc-severity note, not a new assessment: severity stays P4 per the 2026-09-30 ruling.", "acceptance": "npm test completes and vitest summary prints 'N passed' where N is the exact number README.md line ~90 claims as '<N> tests passing'; extracting both with grep -oE '[0-9]+ passed' | head -1 and README grep '<N> tests passing' must return the same N (currently README says 1826, real suite is 1822 passed)."}
