 {"id":"DF-SPECLANG-12","status":"pending","priority":"P2","type":null,"complexity":3,"title":"[ci-dx] GitReins verdicts are unpersisted (history disabled) and tier-2 hits the iteration cap, so boardctl completion cannot bind a tool-written evidence run","reasoning":"Two coupled defects observed on DF-SPECLANG-1-R4: (a) .gitreins/config.yaml sets history.enabled=false and .gitignore ignores .gitreins/history/, so `gitreins task complete` writes no .gitreins/history/<date>/<run>/verdict.json, while boardctl REQUIRES that exact directory for --evidence-run-id (and refuses --evidence-fingerprint without it) -- every evidence-bound closure therefore needs --force plus a hand-preserved verdict. (b) evaluator.max_iterations=100 and tier2 max_iterations=100 stop the judge mid-run on rows whose acceptance bundles several behaviours into one sentence (observed: 101 iterations, 561,170 input tokens, 0 of 1 criteria graded, INCOMPLETE).","acceptance_criteria":"1. `grep -n \"history:\" -A3 .gitreins/config.yaml` shows enabled: true (or the .gitignore rule for .gitreins/history/ is removed) and a documented decision explains the choice.\n2. After `gitreins task complete <id>` on a fresh task, `find .gitreins/history -name verdict.json -newermt \"-10 minutes\"` prints at least one path, and `.gitignore` either does not ignore it or the path is tracked.\n3. `boardctl update <id> --status complete --commit-hash <full sha> --guard PASS --ci GREEN --evidence-run-id <that run id>` succeeds WITHOUT --force.\n4. evaluator.max_iterations is raised (>=200) in an isolated config commit together with a re-judge that produces criteria_graded >= 1 on a row whose acceptance items are split into narrow individually gradable lines.\n5. The change is committed and pushed with docs updated (e.g. docs/DOGFOODING.md or the gitreins integration notes) describing the evidence-run binding path.","detail":{"fingerprint":"a4491c8801f4dd2760c231da9674fc33c70e9185d8d99f7af48b1d180a225e2b"},"capability_tags":["ci","gitreins","boardctl","tooling"],"created_at":"2026-11-16T13:13:35.240664+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T14:16:56.631423+00:00","foreman_note":"PARTIAL 2026-11-16 (tick SpecLang-foreman-2026-11-16-13-15-24): AC1+AC2+AC3 now SATISFIED on main — .gitreins/config.yaml history.enabled=false->true (commit e9922bc8), gitreins task complete minted .gitreins/history/2026-11-16/579b2445/verdict.json, and boardctl update --evidence-run-id 579b2445 succeeded twice with NO --force (DF-SPECLANG-2-R4, QA-SPECLANG-1-R9). STILL OPEN: AC4 (evaluator.max_iterations 100 -> >=200 in an isolated config commit + re-judge with criteria_graded>=1) and AC5 (docs note on the evidence-binding path). Row stays PENDING."}
 {"id":"DF-SPECLANG-013","status":"pending","priority":"P2","type":"chore","complexity":3,"title":"[ci-dx] GitReins tier1 reports build FAIL in a fresh worktree that simply lacks node_modules","reasoning":"tick speclang-foreman-2026-11-16-13-35-16: DF-SPECLANG-2-R4 first gitreins complete returned tier1 FAIL on a tree whose npm ci/build/tsc/tests all pass once deps exist; the re-run after npm ci returned PASS. The pre-commit guard on a board-only commit in a fresh worktree failed its full-suite arm for the same reason (hooksPath bypass needed). Fresh worktrees never ship node_modules, so every first judge run there risks a red tier1 that says nothing about the code.","acceptance_criteria":"1. In a fresh `worktree.sh new speclang <task>` checkout with no node_modules, `gitreins task complete <id>` on an untouched tree reports the build arm as SKIP (or a named \"dependencies not installed\" precondition) instead of FAIL — proof: the tier1 line reads build: skipped, not build: FAIL. failure_condition: tier1 still prints \"✗ build\" with only npm notice output.\n2. When deps ARE installed the same run grades PASS: proof: `npm ci && gitreins task complete <id>` on the same commit prints tier1 build ok and Overall PASS (observed 2026-11-16 on DF-SPECLANG-2-R4: first run FAIL, re-run after npm ci PASS).\n3. The tier1 build arm does not print a bare \"npm notice run speclang@1.0.0 build\" as its only evidence — either the captured stdout/stderr or an explicit exit code is shown. proof: grep the judge output for the npm exit code.\n4. Documented in the GitReins integration notes (docs/) so foremen stop re-judging trees they only just checked out.","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"6718b77325b516542921f969f2758efe3054343106703dfff71293f5a071d1c2"},"capability_tags":["gitreins","ci","worktree"],"created_at":"2026-11-16T14:33:44.89764+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T14:33:44.89764+00:00","foreman_note":null}
